Cost optimization focuses on maximizing the business value obtained from Azure resources while avoiding unnecessary expenditure.

Common cost optimization techniques include:

* Right-sizing resources
* Removing unused resources
* Using appropriate storage tiers
* Autoscaling workloads
* Using budgets and alerts
* Reviewing pricing options
* Scheduling non-production resources
* Monitoring resource utilization

For example, development virtual machines that are only required during working hours can be automatically shut down outside those hours.

A real-life use case is a software company reducing its Azure bill by identifying idle virtual machines and moving infrequently accessed storage data to lower-cost tiers.

Cost optimization should be continuous because workload requirements and resource usage change over time.
